I sit in the flat and take the mobile phone.
I look for the number of my colleague Jonas.
I call him, and he picks up immediately.
"Good morning, Maya," he says cheerfully on the phone.
"Hi Jonas," I answer with a quiet voice.
"Unfortunately, I am not feeling well today."
"I am not coming to the office because I am sick."
Jonas sounds concerned.
"Oh no, what is wrong?" he asks.
"My head hurts," I explain to him.
"My throat also hurts when I speak."
Jonas is very sympathetic.
"Then of course you are not working today," he says.
"You should stay in bed."
"And you should rest."
"Thank you, Jonas," I say and cough a little.
"Get well soon, Maya!" he says kindly.
I end the call and put the mobile phone on the table.
Now I have to call the doctor's practice.
